title: Query engine
tags: Query
kind: overview
audience: dev
summary: How the daemon answers a query — one evaluator over the store's derived key spaces, the forest for the leaves no bitmap holds, a naive oracle to check them.

The daemon has ''one'' query engine: `index::Eval`, generic over a `Source`, whose one
implementation is `KvSource` — the key-value store's derived key spaces
([[Store tables]]). It serves every filter, sort, count and page; there is no SQL and no
fallback ([[No operand runs in SQL]]). Each request reads one snapshot of the store and
nothing stays resident between requests.

A query goes through validation ([[Query validation]]), a preparation in which the
forest resolves paths and rewrites the leaves no bitmap can hold
([[The forest as a query provider]]), the evaluation, and the page
([[How queries are evaluated]]). The store's side of it — the forest's bitmaps, text
search, sorting and postings — is described under [[Storage]].

A second evaluator exists for tests only: [[The query oracle]].

